6. Third-party dependencies

   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md names every dependency declared by a workspace
   manifest with its license, the vendored source, the two pnpm patches applied
   at install time, and the development-only tier. The file is generated:

     pnpm run gen-third-party-notices       rewrite it
     pnpm run verify-third-party-notices    fail when it is stale

   pnpm-lock.yaml pins the whole transitive closure by exact version, and
   `pnpm licenses list` prints the license of every installed package.

   pnpm run verify-dsh-package-licenses checks that every @deepseek-ai/dsh*
   manifest, including this repository's additions, declares "license": "MIT".

   Two facts about distribution:

   - hyperframes (Apache-2.0, github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes) backs
     video_lint, video_snapshot, and video_render. The installed package carries
     no NOTICE file, so Apache-2.0 section 4(d) adds nothing to forward; the
     license text still has to travel with any artifact that bundles the package.
   - The web build copies assets from katex/dist into apps/web/dist/assets/,
     including its font files, without carrying the package's license text.
     katex declares MIT, "Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy and other
     contributors".

   Both gaps are open. Closing them, and the review each one needs before a
   public release, is recorded in
   .agents/notes/proposed/process/2026-10-20-fork-attribution-and-license-map.md.


